{"type":"message","id":"2aaaf95e","parentId":"7b73ddec","timestamp":"2026-03-28T01:38:43.098Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking whether the original image can be saved/stored. Let me think about this - the images sent via Feishu are already saved to `/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/` as shown in the system message. So yes, the original images are stored locally on the Mac.\n\nHowever, the user might be asking about whether the images are stored in the Feishu bitable as well. Currently we're only storing text (the recognized content), not the actual image file itself. \n\nLet me clarify what's happening:\n1. Images sent via Feishu are automatically saved to `/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/` - this is already happening\n2. We're currently only recording the text content in the bitable, not the image itself\n\n\n3. To complete the answer, I should mention that we could also store the image in the bitable using the attachment field type if they wanted to preserve the actual image file rather than just the recognized text.","thinkingSignature":"a87e3a74215167f1dbb7bfd0ac0e611e82f606e1fe3a688a11c5639bd50547be"},{"type":"text","text":"<final>\n\n[[reply_to_current]] 原图会保存在你 Mac 本地：\n\n`/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/`\n\n每次你发图片都会自动存一份，这个不用担心。\n\n---\n\n不过目前录入到飞书多维表格的只是**题目文字**，不是图片本身。\n\n如果你想在飞书里也能看到原图，可以加一个\"原图\"字段（附件类型），把图片也一并存进去。你觉得需要吗？\n\n</final>"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":299,"cacheRead":53724,"cacheWrite":541,"totalTokens":54691,"cost":{"input":0.0000381,"output":0.0003588,"cacheRead":0.0032234399999999997,"cacheWrite":0.000202875,"total":0.0038232149999999996}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774661912774,"responseId":"0616641930085727393e7281cabdb4d3"}}
