{"type":"message","id":"13a4959d","parentId":"95b0b78d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T01:39:26.208Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file exists. Now I need to upload it to Feishu's bitable attachment system. But looking at my tools, I don't have a direct bitable attachment upload API. The bitable attachment field requires file_token from an uploaded file in that bitable.\n\nLet me think... The skill mentions I need to upload the file to the bitable first and get a file_token. But I don't have a dedicated bitable file upload tool in my available tools. \n\nI should inform the user that the attachment field has been added, but uploading images to bitable requires a specific process. For now, the image is stored locally on their Mac, and the bitable stores the text content. \n \nI'm realizing there's a mismatch between what the skill documentation requires and what the current tools support. To properly attach files to bitable records, I'd need to upload to Feishu's file server first and get a token, but that tool doesn't appear to be available. I'll let the user know about this limitation and that they'll need to manually attach images when viewing records in Feishu.","thinkingSignature":"4f9a63297dee4be5a1c81e4796a3619da65f27184fa61cd20abaa43f46037cce"},{"type":"text","text":"\n<final>\n\n[[reply_to_current]] 图片文件在你本地是有的，已经保存好了 ✅\n\n不过飞书的附件字段要求先把图片**上传到飞书服务器**获取 file_token，我目前直接上传这个能力有限。\n\n有两个方案：\n\n**方案 A（推荐）：** 手动在飞书里补充图片\n- 打开刚才那条记录 → 点「原图」字段 → 直接粘贴/上传图片\n\n**方案 B：** 我来搞定自动上传\n- 需要再排查一下上传的流程，确认能走通\n\n---\n\n建议先用方案 A，飞书界面里直接操作也很简单。或者你觉得这个功能重要的话，我们先把方案 B 打通也行。\n\n</final>"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":27416,"output":357,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55765,"cost":{"input":0.008224799999999999,"output":0.0004284,"cacheRead":0.0016795199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01033272}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774661956111,"responseId":"061664446a7c