{"type":"message","id":"fb3d65cf","parentId":"34da06d6","timestamp":"2026-03-28T01:45:28.098Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, actually the upload uses `parent_node` as folder token, not app_token. For bitable, the parent_node needs to be the app_token for bitable-type uploads. But looking at the upload code, it uses `parent_type: 'explorer'` always. Let me try uploading the image file and see what happens.\n\nActually, let me first try to upload to the bitable's folder. But actually, looking at the code more carefully - `parent_type: 'explorer'` is hardcoded, so it always uploads to the file explorer (my space), not to a specific bitable. But the returned file_token should still be usable in the bitable attachment field.\n\nLet me just try uploading and see what happens.","thinkingSignature":"0a35708dffecd9e43a6f69d4da9c936c72d989cd11bc2933d941c6f5df27d094"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":41984,"output":227,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70203,"cost":{"input":0.012595199999999999,"output":0.0002724,"cacheRead":0.0016795199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01454712}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774662321553,"responseId":"061665b1f66726416ff797a2f7eb255f"}}
