{"type":"message","id":"8ab3aabd","parentId":"70dffe9a","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:08:39.344Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - the download action requires a `file_token` and returns the file content. Since our token `boxbcGaNWDdgdGtI2OdljcbTngd` didn't actually result in a real file, the download fails.\n\nLet me step back and think about the actual solution:\n\nThe `feishu_doc_media` tool has a `bitable_upload` action that uploads files to bitable storage specifically for attachment fields. But the attachment field `fldKWDhz1r` was deleted when we switched to the hyperlink approach.\n\nSo the proper flow for the user's requirement should be:\n1. Use `feishu_doc_media` with `bitable_upload` action to upload directly to a bitable attachment field\n\n\n2. But since we already switched to \"原图链接\" (hyperlink), we need a different approach\n\nActually, the user just wants to be able to view the original image when looking at the record. The simplest solution that will actually work is to switch back to attachment field and use the `bitable_upload` action. But we need the attachment field to exist. Let me create the attachment field again and use `bitable_upload` to properly upload the image.\n\nLet me try this:\n1. Create an \"原图\" field (attachment type) - field_id: `fldNEWxxx`\n2. Use `feishu_doc_media` with `bitable_upload` to upload the image and get a proper file_token\n3. Update the record with this new file_token\n\nSo the approach is to first add the attachment field back, then use bitable_upload to properly store the image and get a valid token that won't have the 404 issue.","thinkingSignature":"3a60ee29743d8e71cff7e4f4e641d21fd8f70e06f3ccee4f68129d974e710382"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ma5b75jgvn1q_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_field","arguments":{"action":"create","app_token":"TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1","table_id":"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz","field_name":"原图","type":17}}],"api":"anthropic-messages"