{"type":"message","id":"da4df204","parentId":"f800cf33","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:09:27.751Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload` requires `docs:document.media:upload` and `bitable:app` scopes. These scopes should be available since the user has already authorized the bitable app.\n\nBut the issue is: is `feishu_doc_media` exposed as a callable tool in my current toolset? Looking at the tools listed in the system prompt, I don't see `feishu_doc_media` listed as one of my available tools. \n\nWait - looking at the tool list, there's no `feishu_doc_media` tool listed. So I can't directly call it. \n\nHmm. OK so here's what I know:\n\n\nThe `bitable_upload` approach is available but I can't call it directly. The best path forward is to recreate the attachment field and try updating the record with a properly formatted file_token, though I need to figure out how to get a valid one that bitable will accept.\n\nActually, let me reconsider—maybe I can use the Feishu URL structure directly. The file_token `boxbcGaNWDdgdGtI2OdljcbTngd` might work with a different URL pattern like `https://feishu.cn/drive/file/boxbcGaNWDdgdGtI2OdljcbTngd` rather than what I constructed before.\n\nWait, I already tried that URL and got a 404, which confirms the file doesn't actually exist despite the upload response claiming it succeeded. This looks like a known issue where the `drive:file:upload` API can return a success response without actually creating the file.\n\nI'm thinking I should try the `bitable_upload` approach instead since it has the proper permissions for this operation, though I can't call it directly through the current tool interface. Let me update the user on what I've found so far and ask if they can help invoke it through a different method.\n\nActually, looking back at the file upload code, the issue becomes clearer—the initial upload returns a file_token, but subsequent operations like prepare and