{"type":"message","id":"084a8223","parentId":"49a86856","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:11:19.980Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the plugin structure, it registers tools through the tools/oapi/index.js. The feishu_doc_media tool is registered there.\n\nLet me look at a simpler approach. The issue is that I don't have a tool to call `feishu_doc_media` with `bitable_upload`. But the file.js (feishu_drive_file) DOES support upload and returns file tokens. \n\nActually, let me reconsider the problem. When I called upload using `feishu_drive_file`, it returned a file_token that was a `box...` token. But when trying to access it via feishu.cn/drive/file/box..., it returned 404.\n\nLooking at the upload code again:\n\n\nThe upload endpoint returns a file_token that might be scoped to the uploader's context, so it's not publicly accessible. The `feishu_doc_media` tool with `bitable_upload` is designed specifically to handle this - it takes the file and attaches it to a bitable field rather than just uploading to drive.\n\nI can't directly invoke that tool though. The most straightforward fix would be to add bitable_upload to the tool's description in the source code so it's actually exposed. Since I can't modify the compiled files, I'd need to edit the TypeScript source directly, but I'm not sure if my exec context even has write access to that directory.","thinkingSignature":"37ac1f1053e1143a4fb8b38c243235d64557d0571e77baf551a45e21ea11144f"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_12octsbnp2ny_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la ~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":58624,"output":321,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86937,"cost":{"input":0.0175872,"output":0.0003852,"cacheRead":0.0016795199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01965192}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774663