{"type":"message","id":"17109ad4","parentId":"2baf0124","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:19:52.091Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! It worked! The file was uploaded to bitable's storage and we got a proper file_token: `QgFWbtKEuoX0fFx8s1lcJJ6hnMf`. Now I need to update the record to link this file_token to the correct field.Let me update the record with the new file_token. I need to use the correct record_id and field_id.Actually, looking at this more carefully - when using bitable_upload, the file is uploaded and the token is returned. But I still need to link this to the record. Let me check how this works...\n\nLooking at the bitable_upload code, it seems like the upload goes directly to the bitable storage. But to link it to a record, I still need to use the update_record action with the file_token.\n \nSo the workflow is: I call bitable_upload which returns a file_token, then I need to construct the proper value for the attachment field - it should be an array containing an object with the file_token, like `[{\"file_token\": \"QgFWbtKEuoX0fFx8s1lcJJ6hnMf\"}]`. Let me try updating the record with this format.","thinkingSignature":"9305aff14bf94d787c73db5fa4db24107b82e3be6687f9965ac52c6f0ea6970d"},{"type":"text","text":"上传成功！现在把这个 file_token 写入记录：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_h9g007rq4mxq_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"update","app_token":"TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1","table_id":"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz","record_id":"recvf7BUzqEFSD","fields":{"原图":[{"file_token":"QgFWbtKEuoX0fFx8s1lcJJ6hnMf"}]}}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":59513,"output":394,"cacheRead":34000,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":93907,"cost":{"input":0.0178539,"output":0.0004728,"cacheRead":0.0020399999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.020366699999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774664381452,"responseId":"06166dbd9e2b1fe57e22cf4e342dd993"}}
