{"type":"message","id":"7f351edb","parentId":"70683098","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:32:38.252Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, looking at the logs, the earlier successful call was actually done through the tool calling mechanism (I called feishu_doc_media as a tool and it worked), not via exec+curl to the gateway API. \n\nWait, let me look back at the earlier successful attempt. When I did the math problem image upload, the feishu_doc_media call worked directly. But now when I try the same tool call, it seems to not be going through.\n\nActually wait - in the earlier session, I called the tool directly using `exec` to curl, but looking at the logs it shows `tool call: feishu_doc_media` which means I was calling it as a tool through the normal tool calling mechanism.\n \nLooking at the sequence more carefully: when I attempted to invoke feishu_doc_media via exec+curl, I got a tool-not-found error, but then after updating the description and restarting, the tool call went through successfully and returned a valid file token. Now in this new session it's again not being recognized through the same exec+curl approach, even though the gateway is running. I'm noticing the API endpoint structure changed between sessions—the tool is registered but returning \"Not Found\" on the new port 18789, so I need to track down the correct current endpoint before attempting another upload.","thinkingSignature":"835def810d08e5e1350a823aab725b7a9c5a4cde838157fc573c68bf19b7a767"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_x9u6ge4h49q6_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"18789\\|/rpc\\|/call\\|tool\" /tmp/openclaw/openclaw-2026-03-28.log 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"feishu_doc_media\\|bitable_upload\\|success\\|error\" | tail -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":67926,"output":349,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":96267,"cost":{"input":0.020377799999999998,"output":0.