{"type":"message","id":"ca9a1cf8","parentId":"4354f170","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:32:49.516Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the problem now. The log shows:\n\n```\ntools.allow allowlist contains unknown entries (feishu_create_doc, feishu_doc_comments, feishu_doc_media, feishu_drive_file, ...). These entries won't match any tool unless the plugin is enabled.\n```\n\nThese tools are in the allowlist but the plugin isn't properly enabled for them. Yet in the earlier session, `feishu_doc_media` DID work (I successfully called it and got a result).\n\nSo the question is: why did it work earlier but not now? Looking at the earlier successful calls:\n- `tool call: feishu_doc_media params=...` → `tool done: feishu_doc_media ok (12ms)`\n\n\n- Then another call succeeded in 2654ms\n\nBut now I'm seeing \"unknown tool\" errors. The plugin seems to have been disabled or the allowlist is no longer matching the tool names. I should try calling `feishu_doc_media` directly as a tool rather than going through exec and curl.","thinkingSignature":"c3595714e092aaa61a64fe5ec9c6c6b2b108519a841649403adb74f6631f0583"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_sj54qxpu11yc_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw status 2>/dev/null | head -30"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":76046,"output":252,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":104290,"cost":{"input":0.0228138,"output":0.0003024,"cacheRead":0.0016795199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02479572}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774665158303,"responseId":"061670c678870ff3de303b517777847e"}}
