{"type":"message","id":"4ba6bbba","parentId":"76bb420e","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:33:02.523Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `feishu_doc_media` IS registered. So the tool should be available. The issue is that I'm trying to call it via exec+curl to the gateway API, but the API path is different.\n\nWait, let me look at the log again more carefully. The earlier successful calls show `tool call: feishu_doc_media params=...` followed by `tool done: feishu_doc_media ok`. This means the tool was called directly through the message routing system, not via exec+curl.\n\nSo when I call `feishu_doc_media` as a tool directly (through the messaging system), it works. But when I try to call it via exec+curl to the gateway's HTTP API, it doesn't work.\n\n\nI'm realizing I was overcomplicating this—I don't need to use exec+curl at all. The tool is available through the normal messaging system, so I should just call it directly as a tool, which should work the same way it did before.","thinkingSignature":"1dff5a7afeb6e860584b30dc937672510998ed24e0e2107be91fa80a113702ac"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6ybarr7re5l7_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"echo \"Tool is registered, trying direct approach\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":76933,"output":236,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":105161,"cost":{"input":0.0230799,"output":0.0002832,"cacheRead":0.0016795199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02504262}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774665175438,"responseId":"061670d7d30fa51efd0c69458b0fdb99"}}
