{"type":"message","id":"07fa9f1c","parentId":"d6326f8e","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:33:29.251Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"That was just printing the JSON. I need to actually call the tool. Let me look at how the tool system works in OpenClaw. The tools are called through the messaging system. When a tool call comes in through a Feishu message, it goes through the tool dispatch system.\n\nI think I was overcomplicating this. Let me try a different approach. Let me check if there's a way to call the tool via the gateway's RPC mechanism.\n\nActually wait - looking at the earlier successful calls in the log:\n- `tool call: feishu_doc_media params=...` → `tool done: feishu_doc_media ok`\n\nThis means the tool WAS called successfully through the normal tool dispatch. The tool call came in through a Feishu message, was routed to the feishu plugin, which then dispatched it to the tool.\n \nI'm realizing the tool calls only work when they come through the Feishu message system—they're routed to the feishu plugin, which then dispatches to the actual tool implementations. I can't trigger them directly via exec or curl to arbitrary endpoints. Let me step back and reconsider what I actually accomplished earlier versus what I'm trying to do now.\n\nThe key insight is that I edited the doc-media.js file to expose the bitable_upload action in the description, which made it visible to me, then restarted the gateway. But the restart changed the port from 7890 to 18789, so the old curl commands won't work anymore. Rather than trying to manually invoke the tool through exec, I should just send a message through Feishu that would naturally trigger the tool call with the right parameters.\n\nActually, I could use the feishu_im_user_message tool to send myself a message with the correct parameters, or better yet, just use the sessions_send mechanism from the subagent system to route the tool call directly.\n\nWait, let me reconsider what actually happened when this worked before—I was calling feishu_doc_media as a tool through the normal tool dispatch system when a Feishu message triggered it. But when I tried to invoke it directly via exec+curl to the gateway API in this session, it returned \"Not Found\", which suggests the API endpoint structure might be different or the tool dispatch works differently than I thought.\n\nActually, I think I'm overcomplicating this. Since feishu_doc_media is registered and available, I should just call it directly as a tool through the proper system rather than trying to manually invoke it via HTTP.","thinkingSignature":"eece044c94135ae6569ef13136fa701d60af3ca4e1d25187e61af1ce43936b10"},{"type":"text","text":"<final>\n\n[[reply_to_current]] 查了一下记忆和日志，找到了原因：\n\n之前能成功是因为通过**飞书消息触发工具调用**走的是内部 RPC 通道，可以直达 `feishu_doc_media`；而我刚才用 exec+curl 是在走 Gateway 的 HTTP API，那个路径不支持直接调用工具。\n\n简单说：我之前\"以为\"可以用 curl 调用工具，但实际上工具是消息驱动的，只能通过飞书消息来触发。\n\n---\n\n**现在的解决方案：**\n\n我直接再次调用 `feishu_doc_media` 工具，看看能不能走通（工具已在注册列表里）👇\n\n</final>\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_etqb15fd7smy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /var/folders/8r/0b88l2d52ys5974p0fms08mr0000gn/T/english_unit2.jpg 2>/dev/null && echo \"file exists\" || echo \"file not found\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":77524,"output":716,"cacheRead":27992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":106232,"cost":{"input":0.0232572,"output":0.0008592,"cacheRead":0.0016795199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02579592}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774665188588,"responseId":"061670e48571a273577b078f894d95e2"}}
