{"type":"message","id":"8419a728","parentId":"0a04db23","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:33:41.024Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK the file exists. But I still need a way to call feishu_doc_media. Let me try a different approach - I'll try calling the tool directly. The tool should be available through the normal tool dispatch system.\n\nActually, I realize now that when I call a tool directly (not through exec), it goes through the tool dispatch system. Let me try calling it through the sessions_spawn mechanism.\n\nWait, I think I need to just send a message to myself that triggers the tool. But actually, the cleanest approach is to try calling feishu_doc_media directly as a tool. Since it's registered, it should appear as an available tool. Let me just try calling it.\n\nBut wait - I'm the assistant running in the main session. The tools I have access to are the ones listed in the system prompt. feishu_doc_media is NOT in my tool list - it's only registered in the OpenClaw plugin system.\n \nSo the issue is that feishu_doc_media is registered in the plugin but not exposed to me as a callable tool. When I tried using exec to call it directly, I got errors - exit code 7 from curl indicating connection refused, and a 404 from the gateway API.\n\nThe real solution is to route the call through Feishu messages instead, using the feishu_im_user_message tool to send a message that triggers the tool dispatch. Alternatively, I could try using sessions_spawn to handle the image processing task.","thinkingSignature":"2e048affd2bbc9b7e3158b3a4d70c8e8a4be7b4a3e74a358729b595ed5db5b98"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_y40a5i2yjgbt_1","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"task":"请帮我调用 feishu_doc_media 工具，action=bitable_upload，参数如下：\n- app_token: TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\n- table_id: tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\n- field_id: fld2F4ad3r\n- file_path: /var/folders/8r/0b88l2d52ys5974p0fms08mr0000gn/T/english_unit2.jpg\n- type: image\n\n把返回的 file_to