{"type":"message","id":"66d6375f","parentId":"3f24bcde","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:49:13.280Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The feishu_doc_media tool isn't being triggered. I think the issue is that I need to actually use the tool in a call, not just echo. Let me think about this differently.\n\nThe feishu_doc_media tool is registered and available. When I call it (either directly in my response or through a proper tool call), it should work. But when I try to call it, I get no response or an error.\n\nWait, I think the problem is that when I try to use feishu_doc_media by putting it in my tool calls, it actually does get called but returns an error. The error is \"WrongRequestBody\" when trying to update the record with the wrong file_token.\n \nI'm realizing I haven't actually invoked feishu_doc_media yet in this conversation—I've only tried to work around it. When I do call it, I need to use the correct field format for bitable attachments, where the file_token comes from bitable_upload and gets passed as an array with the right structure.\n\nThe file is already at the correct temp path, so if I can get feishu_doc_media to actually execute, it should return the right token. But I'm still getting the \"tool not found\" or \"action requires invoke\" error when I try to invoke it directly, which suggests something's off with how the tool is being registered or called.","thinkingSignature":"fd3181bb8214097e3547bb2f848d8acc2d21bfa149af2e7193c309ff2d9ab643"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_yyo6j1f8hulo_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"echo \"test feishu_doc_media\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":86937,"output":312,"cacheRead":28383,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":115632,"cost":{"input":0.0260811,"output":0.0003744,"cacheRead":0.0017029799999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02815848}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774666142051,"responseId":"0616749e82