{"type":"message","id":"1b6aac35","parentId":"27b9ca3d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:54:27.143Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 404. Let me check if the API endpoint is correct. The SDK uses `sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll` - let me check what the actual HTTP endpoint is.Actually, looking at the lark SDK source... let me look at the file.js to see what endpoint it calls.Actually, looking at the Feishu API docs, the upload endpoint is `POST /open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all`. But maybe for bitable specific uploads, the endpoint is different.Wait, maybe the issue is that for bitable uploads, the `parent_type` should be `bitable` instead of `bitable_file`? Let me check what the doc-media.js uses.Actually, looking at the handleBitableUpload function in doc-media.js:```javascript\nconst parentType = 'bitable';\n...\n\n\nextra: JSON.stringify({\n    bitablePerm: {\n        tableId: p.table_id,\n    },\n}),\n```So parent_type should be 'bitable'. But looking at the Feishu API docs more carefully, `parent_type` for bitable files should actually be `bitable_file`. Let me try with a different approach - maybe the issue is that I'm using the wrong API path. Let me try `https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/med`.\n\nLooking at the error more carefully, I think the problem might be that the access token doesn't have the right scopes for bitable uploads. The `bitable_upload` scope might not be included. Let me check what scopes are needed - the tool-scopes.js shows it requires `docs:document.media:upload` and `bitable:app`, so maybe I need to verify the token has these permissions. But the \"page not found\" error suggests the endpoint itself isn't being found, not a scope issue.\n\nLooking at the available API versions, the current version is `v2`, and `v1` might be deprecated. Let me try `https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v2/media/upload_all` instead.\n\nThe Feishu SDK also supports configuring custom API domain hosts via `domain` parameter, so maybe the issue is that I'm hitting the wrong base URL. Let me try a simpler test first - just check if the basic upload endpoint responds at all.","thinkingSignature":"1311102cedc87ef30b1f2da385e10cb92e30968b62477fb5d81f043f13891b00"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_zwwsbc424uyc_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"FULL_TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s \"openclaw-feishu-uat\" -a \"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\" -w 2>/dev/null)\nACCESS_TOKEN=$(echo \"$FULL_TOKEN\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('accessToken',''))\")\n\n# Try v2 endpoint\ncurl -v \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=test.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_file\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F \"size=100\" \\\n  -F \"file=@/var/folders/8r/0b88l2d52ys5974p0fms08mr0000gn/T/math_inequality.jpg;type=image/jpeg\" \\\n  -F 'extra={\"bitablePerm\":{\"tableId\":\"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\"}}' 2>&1 | tail -20","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":96647,"output":784,"cacheRead":28383,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":125814,"cost":{"input":0.0289941,"output":0.0009408,"cacheRead":0.0017029799999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03163787999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774666445851,"responseId":"061675ce14762fa029f6ddc6d678d3a3"}}
