{"type":"message","id":"d22b1f7a","parentId":"11350260","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:54:55.747Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_5hpd26k9jr20_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"async function handleBitableUpload(p, client, log) {\n    const filePath = p.file_path;\n    const mediaType = p.type ?? 'image';\n    const DOC_MEDIA_ALLOWED_ROOTS = [os.tmpdir()];\n    (0, media_url_utils_1.validateLocalMediaRoots)(path.resolve(filePath), DOC_MEDIA_ALLOWED_ROOTS);\n    let fileSize;\n    try {\n        const stat = await fs.stat(filePath);\n        fileSize = stat.size;\n    }\n    catch (err) {\n        return (0, helpers_1.json)({\n            error: `failed to read file: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`,\n        });\n    }\n    if (fileSize > MAX_FILE_SIZE) {\n        return (0, helpers_1.json)({\n            error: `file ${(fileSize / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)}MB exceeds 20MB limit`,\n        });\n    }\n    const fileName = path.basename(filePath);\n    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    // 读取文件内容作为 Buffer 传递\n    const fileBuffer = await fs.readFile(filePath);\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: p.app_token,\n            size: fileSize,\n--\n                    return await handleBitableUpload(p, client, log);\n                }\n                return (0, helpers_1.json)({ error: `unknown action: ${p.action}` });\n            }\n            catch (err) {\n                return await (0, helpers_1.handleInvokeErrorWithAutoAuth)(err, cfg);\n            }\n        },"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":15,"aggregated":"async function handleBitableUpload(p, client, log) {\n    const filePath = p.file_path;\n    const mediaType = p.type ?? 'image';\n    const DOC_MEDIA_ALLOWED_ROOTS = [os.tmpdir()];\n    (0, media_url_utils_1.validateLocalMediaRoots)(path.resolve(filePath), DOC_MEDIA_ALLOWED_ROOTS);\n    let fileSize;\n    try {\n        const stat = await fs.stat(filePath);\n        fileSize = stat.size;\n    }\n    catch (err) {\n        return (0, helpers_1.json)({\n            error: `failed to read file: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`,\n        });\n    }\n    if (fileSize > MAX_FILE_SIZE) {\n        return (0, helpers_1.json)({\n            error: `file ${(fileSize / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)}MB exceeds 20MB limit`,\n        });\n    }\n    const fileName = path.basename(filePath);\n    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    // 读取文件内容作为 Buffer 传递\n    const fileBuffer = await fs.readFile(filePath);\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: p.app_token,\n            size: fileSize,\n--\n                    return await handleBitableUpload(p, client, log);\n                }\n                return (0, helpers_1.json)({ error: `unknown action: ${p.action}` });\n            }\n            catch (err) {\n                return await (0, helpers_1.handleInvokeErrorWithAutoAuth)(err, cfg);\n            }\n        },","cwd":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774666495740}}
{"type":"message","id":"b65eb1c3","parentId":"d22b1f7a","timestamp":"2026-03-28T02:55:11.379Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! The `parentType` for images is `'bitable_image'`, not `'bitable_file'`! And importantly, I also see it uses `sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll` which is the same API I'm calling. But the key difference is that the SDK passes the data differently.\n\nAlso, importantly, the `handleBitableUpload` function uses `client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', ...)` which goes through the OpenClaw's SDK invocation mechanism, not a raw HTTP call. The OpenClaw SDK might have a different base URL or transport mechanism.\n\nWait, but when I use curl directly with the same API endpoint and auth, it should work...\n \nI think the issue might be that the Feishu SDK in the OpenClaw plugin uses a different domain for API calls than the standard `open.feishu.cn`. The connectionMode is \"websocket\" which suggests it might be using a different transport. Let me try checking if there's a way to see what domain the SDK is actually configured to use.\n\nActually, the real problem is that I was using `parent_type=bitable_file` when the correct value for images should be `parent_type=bitable_image`. That's why the upload is failing. Let me retry with the correct parameter.","thinkingSignature":"0f0fe70301c3555b7bb2b442d4ddc2caa7f0e9aa0348bdcac867281ae7da9b62"},{"type":"text","text":"发现问题了！图片的 `parent_type` 应该是 `bitable_image`，不是 `bitable_file`：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_gktoxrapoqhe_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"FULL_TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s \"openclaw-feishu-uat\" -a \"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\" -w 2>/dev/null)\nACCESS_TOKEN=$(echo \"$FULL_TOKEN\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('accessToken',''))\")\n\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=math_inequality.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F \"size=235941\" \\\n  -F \"file=@/var/folders/8r/0b88l2d52ys5974p0fms08mr0000gn/T/math_inequality.jpg;type=image/jpeg\" \\\n  -F 'extra={\"bitablePerm\":{\"tableId\":\"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\"}}'","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":99324,"output":594,"cacheRead":28383,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":128301,"cost":{"input":0.0297972,"output":0.0007128,"cacheRead":0.0017029799999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03221298}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774666495749,"responseId":"06167600343ab98647d07ab5c3a6f73d"}}
