{"type":"message","id":"1fc1e34d","parentId":"afd28851","timestamp":"2026-03-28T06:41:33.358Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the records from the old bitable. Let me analyze the field structure:\n\nOld bitable fields:\n- 科目 (subject) - Single select\n- 题目 (question content) - Text\n- 正确答案 (correct answer) - Text\n- 错误答案 (wrong answer) - Text\n- 知识点 (knowledge points) - Text (stored as text, not multi-select)\n- 掌握程度 (mastery level) - Number (0/1/2)\n- 错题日期 (date) - Date\n- 附件 (attachment) - Attachment\n\n\n- New bitable fields:\n- 学科 (subject) - Single select\n- 题目内容 (question content) - Text\n- 正确答案 (correct answer) - Text\n- 错因分析 (error analysis) - Text\n- 知识点 (knowledge points) - Multi-select\n- 难度 (difficulty) - Single select\n- 录入时间 (entry time) - Date\n- 备注 (notes) - Text\n- 原图 (original image) - Attachment\n\nI need to map the old fields to the new structure: 科目 becomes 学科, 题目 maps to 题目内容, and the knowledge points field will need to be converted from text format to the multi-select format. Now I'm organizing the records and need to handle image attachments carefully since the existing tool for attaching images to records has been unreliable. I'll prepare all 8 records for migration and attempt to upload the images with fallback options if the primary tool doesn't work, then create the batch insert request. Looking at the records, I can see the math problem has geometry rotation and isosceles triangles, the English questions involve present perfect tense versus simple past tense and non-continuous verbs with for/since, and geography covers Qinghai-Tibet agriculture and Taiwan geography.\n\nNow I'm examining the physics problems—绳断受力分析 and another mechanics question on 力与运动—then planning the import strategy. I'll batch create all 8 records at once, handling the image attachment as a special case since I already have the old token. The key distinction is whether these are truly old records needing migration or newly created entries, which affects whether I should preserve the original dates or use the current timestamp.\n\nI'll use the old record dates and try to download and re-upload the images through the proper bitable API. For the knowledge points, I'll map them from the old text format into multi-select options, converting things like \"几何旋转\" to the standardized select format even if they don't perfectly match the new system's categories. I notice the physics records are missing mastery level data, so I'll handle those with a default value.\n\nNow I'm checking the new bitable's knowledge points field to see what options are actually available. The current setup has some math categories like 一次函数 and 全等三角形, but I need to verify which ones match the imported data and identify any gaps like 几何旋转 that might need to be added as new options.\n\nI'm realizing the import will be messy regardless—some old categories won't map cleanly to the new structure, and I'll have to manually add new select options. My best approach is to do a batch import first, create missing knowledge point options during the process, and flag any records with unmapped categories for later cleanup. Looking at what needs to be added: 几何旋转, 现在完成时, 非延续性动词, 青藏地区农业, and 台湾岛自然地理特征 are all new. The knowledge points field is multiple select, so I can include both old and new categories together in the import. Now I'm ready to execute the batch create and check the actual field structure from the old bitable to ensure the data maps correctly.\n\nThe old fields are straightforward—single select for subject, text for the question content and answers, a text array for knowledge points, a number for mastery level, a date field, and attachments. I'll use the correct record IDs and submit the batch create request now, letting the system add missing select options automatically where needed.","thinkingSignature":"9abab6b7040697b5fd46e6ad724e3c638a087c417b397f44d6ac8912c08ae005"},{"type":"text","text":"旧表有8条记录，结构和新表不完全一样，我来整理一下然后批量迁移：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_o371t9fofqso_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_field","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1","table_id":"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":117356,"output":918,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":146658,"cost":{"input":0.035206799999999996,"output":0.0011015999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03801144}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774680056804,"responseId":"0616aaf918dc5241a1daeb032a7b248f"}}
