{"type":"message","id":"60e7f6e6","parentId":"f3cac165","timestamp":"2026-03-28T08:03:29.548Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PDF content is heavily compressed/encoded. The strings command shows binary content, not readable text. This is because the PDF uses internal compression.\n\nLet me try using `sips` to convert the pages to images, and then use the image tool to read the actual content. But wait - earlier when I tried this, all pages showed the cover page. This might be because the PDF was created with a cover page template where all pages look similar, or the PDF conversion tool on macOS is not working correctly for this specific PDF.\n\nLet me try one more approach - using the `pdf` to image conversion but on specific page numbers.","thinkingSignature":"013b059f593f3b973f93f586e9d96271bf3e18bd6c4d8361a2b13ead33f04c58"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_hoa61yx52rn0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try using macOS built-in PDF thumbnail generation for different pages\n# Use the built-in PDF framework via Python\npython3 << 'EOF'\nfrom CoreGraphics import PDFDocument, PDFPage\nimport Cocoa\n\nurl = Cocoa.NSURL.fileURLWithPath_(\"/tmp/biology.pdf\")\npdf_doc = PDFDocument.alloc().initWithURL_(url)\n\nif pdf_doc:\n    print(f\"Total pages: {pdf_doc.pageCount()}\")\n    # Try to get text from first page\n    page = pdf_doc.pageAtIndex_(0)\n    if page:\n        text = page.string()\n        if text:\n            print(f\"Page 1 text (first 500 chars): {text[:500]}\")\n        else:\n            print(\"Page 1 has no extractable text\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Failed to open PDF\")\nEOF"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":129982,"output":327,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":158693,"cost":{"input":0.0389946,"output":0.0003924,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.04109004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":177468499577