{"type":"message","id":"0163c39d","parentId":"91e0a703","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:44:45.260Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting \"params error\". The issue might be with the extra parameter format. Let me try stringifying the extra differently, or maybe the issue is with the file path or file format. Let me check the file exists and try with a simpler approach.\n\nActually, the problem might be that the file path in the -F flag should just be @/tmp/geography_q25.jpg without the ;type= part. Let me also try without the extra.bitablePerm parameter first to see if the basic upload works, though without the bitable perm the file won't be accessible in the bitable context.\n\nWait - the issue might be with the parent_node format. For bitable, the parent_node should be the app token, which I provided correctly. \n\nThe \"params error\" could mean the file is too large, the format is wrong, or the bitable perm is incorrect. Let me test uploading to drive first without the bitable-specific parameters to isolate whether it's a file issue or a permission issue.","thinkingSignature":"9edc14f1aa61a472eca42de32a2d6ac67f34baf4b595d3a356d473a4876c8012"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ybpxskup86ma_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Try without extra.bitablePerm first to test basic upload\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=geography_q25.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"file_type=image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F \"file=@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax