{"type":"message","id":"2bf9fcfc","parentId":"5540660b","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:44:57.291Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still \"params error\" even without the extra. The issue might be with the parent_type value. Let me check - for bitable images, the parent_type should be \"bitable_image\" or \"bitable_file\". Actually the docs say for bitable it should be `bitable_file` for files and `bitable_image` for images.\n\nBut wait - I'm getting \"params error\" which might mean the file itself is problematic, or the file_type is wrong. Let me check the file size and try with a very simple test.\n\nActually, I think the issue might be that I'm not supposed to use bitable_image directly - maybe the API expects a different parent_type for the upload_all endpoint when targeting bitable. \n\nLet me try switching to `drive.v1.media.uploadAll` instead, or test with a basic text file to see if the upload_all endpoint works at all.","thinkingSignature":"623625ab14f6c33654a5274567bfded05ed841d9977438f28d9a7fd23600459c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_4l50s3znr4se_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Test with a simple text file first\necho \"test\" > /tmp/test.txt\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=test.txt\" \\\n  -F \"file_type=stream\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_file\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F \"file=@/tmp/test.txt\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":57295,"output":423,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86102,"cost":{"input":0.0171885,"output":0.0005076,"cacheRead