{"type":"message","id":"f283803f","parentId":"2bf9fcfc","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:44:57.577Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_4l50s3znr4se_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"code\":1061002,\"msg\":\"params error.\",\"error\":{\"log_id\":\"20260328224457D2B488ACE6286E6D4ADF\",\"troubleshooter\":\"排查建议查看(Troubleshooting suggestions): https://open.feishu.cn/search?from=openapi&log_id=20260328224457D2B488ACE6286E6D4ADF&code=1061002&method_id=6944991842538766337\"}}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":242,"aggregated":"{\"code\":1061002,\"msg\":\"params error.\",\"error\":{\"log_id\":\"20260328224457D2B488ACE6286E6D4ADF\",\"troubleshooter\":\"排查建议查看(Troubleshooting suggestions): https://open.feishu.cn/search?from=openapi&log_id=20260328224457D2B488ACE6286E6D4ADF&code=1061002&method_id=6944991842538766337\"}}","cwd":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774709097570}}
{"type":"message","id":"32a95dc8","parentId":"f283803f","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:45:10.090Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even a simple text file gives the same error. The issue is likely with the Authorization header or the request format itself. Let me check the token extraction more carefully - maybe the issue is that the token is somehow truncated or has extra whitespace.\n\nWait, looking at the code 1061002 - this seems to be a lark API error for \"params error\". This could mean:\n1. The Authorization header format is wrong\n2. The file field name is wrong\n3. Some required parameter is missing\n\nLet me try a slightly different curl format. The -F flag in curl should work... Let me check if maybe it's an issue with the curl version or the way the file is being sent.\n\n\nActually, I think the real problem might be how the file path is being resolved. When I use `@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg` in curl, the shell should expand that correctly, but maybe the file path itself is the issue here.\n\nLet me try switching to the media API upload endpoint instead - that might handle the file attachment differently for bitable contexts.","thinkingSignature":"bdb75e2ec8ba95e8bf43ad17ab8a6e52ac02bef23afd57d3a414ad286701aeb0"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0ei66yjrh1ef_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Try media/uploadAll endpoint\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=geography_q25.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"file_type=image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F \"extra={\\\"bitablePerm\\\":{\\\"tableId\\\":\\\"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\\\",\\\"fieldId\\\":\\\"fld2F4ad3r\\\",\\\"recordId\\\":\\\"recvfaO6GVjeG4\\\"}}\" \\\n  -F \"file=@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg;type=image/jpeg\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":57835,"output":510,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86729,"cost":{"input":0.017350499999999998,"output":0.000612,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01966554}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709097578,"responseId":"06171c6990d0434e4ba07e0525580e45"}}
