{"type":"message","id":"3aae2745","parentId":"0180a45b","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:45:22.276Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"404 on the media endpoint. The endpoint should be `https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all`. Actually wait - the correct endpoint for media upload is `https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all`. But I'm getting 404 which means the URL is wrong or the method doesn't exist.\n\nLet me try the correct URL format. Looking at the lark docs, the upload endpoint is:\n`POST https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all`\n\nBut my curl is getting \"params error\" which is a specific API error, not a 404. The 404 I just got was for the media endpoint.\n \nI should go back to the working endpoint that produced the \"params error\" - that's the files/upload_all one. Let me try building the curl request with explicit newlines and verbose output to see exactly what's being sent.","thinkingSignature":"45727cbe4c07e710e0aeb1cc23498a16480546dd8ac04c90de4b957d4784f840"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_n2iyz33d6oy1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\ncurl -v -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}\" \\\n  -H \"Expect:\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=geography_q25.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"file_type=image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F 'extra={\"bitablePerm\":{\"tableId\":\"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\",\"fieldId\":\"fld2F4ad3r\",\"recordId\":\"recvfaO6GVjeG4\"}}' \\\n  -F \"file=@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg\" 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input