{"type":"message","id":"e7d11a28","parentId":"a9ca0924","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:46:21.669Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Same error even without the extra. The issue must be with the parent_node or the Authorization. Let me think... \n\nWait, looking at the previous successful upload from the conversation, it used a file_token and I was able to update records. The issue might be that the token I'm using doesn't have the `drive:file:upload` scope, even though it has many other scopes. Let me check the token scopes again...\n\nActually wait - looking at the token carefully, I see the scope includes `drive:file:upload` - yes: `ImFtZTpjaGF0LmFjY2Vzc19ldmVudC5ib3RfcDJwX2NoYXQ6cmVhZCBpbTpjaGF0OnJlYWQgaW06b...` and more. \n\nSo `drive:file:upload` IS in the scope. The scopes are space-separated, and I can see it listed there. So the scope isn't the problem. Maybe I'm using the wrong API endpoint - the docs mention `drive.v1.media.uploadAll` for bitable uploads, so let me try switching to that instead.","thinkingSignature":"278800b7fcbc7299931cda4bbb1d4436ff879462303208974cef7d9f3bb8b201"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cnx6gee6nnh2_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Try the media endpoint with correct path\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/media/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=geography_q25.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"file_type=jpeg\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_file\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F 'extra={\"bitablePerm\":{\"tableId\":\"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\",\"fieldId\":\"fld2F4ad3r\",\"recordId\":\"recvfaO6GVjeG4\"}}' \\\n  -F \"file=@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg;type=image/jpeg\""}}],