{"type":"message","id":"3fef43c9","parentId":"cb462987","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:47:17.786Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `/drive/v1/media/upload_all` endpoint returns 404, so it doesn't exist. The correct endpoint is `/drive/v1/files/upload_all`.\n\nI'm consistently getting `params error` with `code: 1061002`. Let me think about what could be different...\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the previous successful run in the conversation history (around line 8 in the summary), it mentions:\n```\n- 最终发现正确方案:直接从 Keychain 拿 user access_token → 调 `https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all` + `extra.bitablePerm`\n\n\n```\n\nBut the actual API call isn't shown in detail. Let me check if maybe the problem is the file_name encoding - it contains Chinese characters (geography_q25.jpg contains no Chinese, but the file was originally named with Chinese characters before copying). No wait, the copy renamed it to geography_q25.jpg which is ASCII.\n\nHmm, let me try with a simple text file again but this time with a proper file path and see if the issue is actually the file content or the way curl is sending it. Actually, let me try adding `-v` to curl to see exactly what's being sent. I've already done this and can see the file size is being logged, so the file is being uploaded.\n\nWait - I notice the server's `x-lgw-dst-svc` header is `rtjg3lGvTlGe0b3JMB4yleVsqM-fbHJQVQoyPFI2eGw3UcpxcfYOzrN8tyAlRjQF8UO_I776_ekezwekMC_eGbgZtzFDmglsOsaLrTrAaqFIupwOEametNFw-iak1KOa61doI40SMBQQf-mCXNb9U8mESgBPsRVVAF3M6Wt3AWfu39ly-PtXI-Si8fZ5589TsG98dH_7VOXGkemxdZ1Kv06hS3qXuJ5aieu-fmEGTEWJvyGSqo_Up9E9tQ9nxE3raMnIT3uOVXxHCJAxmDnsCP4K8nu1O6yNovZjW81ndIAh7f__jvWn9Vjqt06U221YwXNY9\n\n```\n\nThis header is unusual - it might be an API gateway header. The request IS reaching the Feishu server (I can see response headers), but I'm getting a \"params error\" response. Looking at the curl output, the request body shows `100  205k` which means the file IS being sent (205k bytes). If the file wasn't being read properly or the file field was wrong, I'd expect a different error like \"file is required\" or \"file not found\". Since I'm getting a params error specifically, the file is being received but something about the parameters is wrong.\n\nI'm realizing this might be a token issue - specifically with how the extra.bitablePerm JSON is being formatted in the shell. When I use single quotes around the JSON in curl with `-F \"extra=...\"`, the shell should pass it literally without variable expansion since there are no `$` characters in the JSON string, so that should be fine. But let me double-check the shell command being executed to make sure the JSON structure is correct.\n\nActually, maybe the problem isn't the curl command at all. Since the record was created successfully earlier, perhaps the bitable attachment field just doesn't accept direct file uploads through the API - maybe it only works through the UI. Or if it does work via API, there might be a different endpoint or method I should be using. Let me try a simpler approach and see if I can add the file token directly to the record instead of uploading it.\n\nThe extra.bitablePerm in the upload call was supposed to set permissions so the file is accessible to the bitable app, but if that upload is failing, maybe the workaround is to upload the file without those permissions and then manually grant access afterward, though I'm not sure what API call would handle that second step. I'm starting to think the upload is failing because the token might not have sufficient permissions for this operation.\n\nLooking at the error response again - \"params error\" with no more details - this could mean the file itself has an issue, the parent_node is invalid, or the extra JSON is malformed. But since I'm pretty confident the token is correct from the keychain, the parent_node matches the app_token, and the extra looks right, maybe I should try creating a fresh token from the keychain to see if the existing one has degraded.\n\nActually, let me step back - maybe I'm overcomplicating this. If the upload keeps failing, I could just skip the image attachment for now and tell the user the text was saved successfully. Or I could try using the feishu_im_bot_image tool to download the image and re-upload it differently. But wait, looking at the record creation, the text-only version worked fine, so maybe the user will be okay without the image. Though they did explicitly ask to add the original image.\n\nLet me try uploading via a different method - maybe Python requests with proper multipart form encoding instead of curl's -F flag.","thinkingSignature":"7393fe0ec935717a2c96cf8679ceff963172a139ffcd77db0db51a665c396296"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_d313axam7ien_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\npython3 << 'EOF'\nimport requests\nimport json\n\ntoken = \"eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsImZlYXR1cmVfY29kZSI6IkZlYXR1cmVPQXV0aEpXVFNpZ25fQ04iLCJraWQiOiI3NjIwOTc2NDA5MTExMjkzMTM4IiwidHlwIjoiSldUIn0..Ns3myd4k-EIJfZcBVsJsMsp2i_jcQ_EShXGrStPp439AvrOL1srYRXy1lCEh25xJ3yAjTp6Wqgss4Gz88CvVdg\"\n\nurl = \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all\"\n\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"\n}\n\nfiles = {\n    \"file_name\": \"geography_q25.jpg\",\n    \"file_type\": \"image\",\n    \"parent_type\": \"bitable_image\",\n    \"parent_node\": \"TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\",\n    \"extra\": json.dumps({\"bitablePerm\": {\"tableId\": \"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz\", \"fieldId\": \"fld2F4ad3r\", \"recordId\": \"recvfaO6GVjeG4\"}})\n}\n\nwith open(\"/tmp/geography_q25.jpg\", \"rb\") as f:\n    files[\"file\"] = (\"geography_q25.jpg\", f, \"image/jpeg\")\n    \n    response = request