{"type":"message","id":"81a71e6d","parentId":"b089d024","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:47:55.037Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! Now I get \"Invalid access token\" with the Python approach, but the curl approach was getting \"params error\". This is strange because both should use the same token. \n\nWait - looking at the Python code, I hardcoded the token string but it might have gotten truncated or altered. The token in the Python script is the same one from the keychain but it might have been truncated when I copy-pasted it into the heredoc.\n\nLet me use the TOKEN variable from the shell instead:","thinkingSignature":"d002e57d088fc61016e88e402e4b84d4401ff12dbc28ca5e573f72a10d6e0e6d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_a5cuyrvs16ut_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\necho \"Token starts with: ${TOKEN:0:50}\"\necho \"Token ends with: ${TOKEN: -50}\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":67319,"output":244,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":95947,"cost":{"input":0.0201957,"output":0.00029279999999999996,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02219154}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709268526,"responseId":"06171d140597a091da8369af65e19652"}}
