{"type":"message","id":"74810b58","parentId":"65c479d7","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:48:32.998Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now we're back to the same \"params error\" with the Python approach. But this is different from the curl approach where we got \"Invalid access token\" with Python's urllib. Interesting.\n\nLet me think about this differently. Maybe the issue is with the extra.bitablePerm format. Let me look at what the correct format should be.\n\nActually, let me look at the successful upload that happened in the earlier session more carefully. From the summary: \"最终发现正确方案:直接从 Keychain 拿 user access_token → 调 `https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all` + `extra.bitablePerm`\"\n\nAnd from the MEMORY.md:\n\n\nI'm noticing something odd here - the user access token was used successfully in the previous session with the exact same API endpoint, but now it's returning a \"params error\" for both curl and Python. This makes me wonder if the record ID for the newly created entry is different or if the table/field IDs have changed since then.\n\nLooking at the IDs across both sessions, they appear consistent - the app token, table ID, and field ID all match what was used before. But I'm realizing the core issue might be with how the bitable API is handling file tokens versus image tokens when updating records. When I successfully created the record initially, it was empty, and now I'm trying to add an image to that same record.\n\nLet me reconsider the `parent_type` parameter - maybe it shouldn't be `bitable_image` at all, or perhaps there's a different approach using the `drive.v1.media.upload_all` endpoint that the Feishu documentation mentions. Though the 404 error I got earlier suggests that endpoint might not be the right path either.\n\nI'm going in circles here. Let me step back - the record is already saved without the image attached, so maybe that's acceptable. But the user did specifically request the image be included, so I should explore whether there's a way to batch update the attachment field in a single API call instead of trying to upload the file separately first. I'm realizing the core issue: maybe I need to upload the file first without the bitable perm to get a file token, then use that token when updating the record field separately. Let me test uploading without the bitable perm parameter to see if that works, though I suspect the token might not have the right permissions for that operation.","thinkingSignature":"237d62210b3e2d21604ca29f692144f30d586f7859b8601b56e710ce480a8909"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_47lsi7xr1601_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Try uploading to mypermspace first (simpler parent)\npython3 - << PYEOF\nimport urllib.request\nimport json\n\ntoken = \"\"\"${TOKEN}\"\"\"\n\nurl = \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all\"\n\nboundary = \"----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW\"\n\nwith open(\"/tmp/geography_q25.jpg\", \"rb\") as f:\n    file_content = f.read()\n\nbody = f\"\"\"--{boundary}\\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file_name\"\\r\n\\r\ngeography_q25.jpg\\r\n--{boundary}\\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file_type\"\\r\n\\r\nimage\\r\n--{boundary}\\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"parent_type\"\\r\n\\r\nmypermspace\\r\n--{boundary}\\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"geography_q25.jpg\"\\r\nContent-Type: image/jpeg\\r\n\\r\n\"\"\".encode('utf-8') + file_content + f\"\\r\\n--{boundary}--\\r\\n\".encode('utf-8')\n\nreq = urllib.request.Request(\n    url,\n    data=body,\n    headers={\n        \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n        \"Content-Type\": f\"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}\"\n    },\n    method=\"POST\"\n)\n\ntry:\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as response:\n        result = response.read().decode('utf-8')\n        print(f\"Status: {response.status}\")\n        print(f\"Response: {result}\")\nexcept urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n    print(f\"HTTP Error: {e.code}\")\n    print(f\"Body: {e.read().decode('utf-8')}\")\nPYEOF"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":68414,"output":982,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":97780,"cost":{"input":0.0205242,"output":0.0011784,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02340564}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709288935,"responseId":"06171d2997c8a7d6e156468b580977d8"}}
