{"type":"message","id":"61e5b631","parentId":"68a6a15a","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:49:31.522Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `feishu_doc_media` tool with `bitable_upload` action exists in the source code! But it wasn't showing up in my available tools list. This might be because the Gateway needs to be restarted or the tool registry needs to be refreshed.\n\nHowever, since this is running in the main session context (not a subagent), the tool should theoretically be available. But based on my tooling results, I don't see it listed.\n\nLet me try to directly invoke the tool by calling it through the exec tool - but that's not how tools work. Tools are invoked by the AI calling them, not by exec.\n\nWait - looking at the tools list again from the system prompt, I don't see `feishu_doc_media` in the available tools. This might be a session context issue where the tool isn't registered in this particular session.\n\n\nThe plugin might not be fully initialized in this session even though the file exists. Rather than trying to invoke the tool directly, I could write a script that imitates what the tool does internally - using curl to call the Feishu API with the user access token from the keychain and the upload endpoint. But I've already attempted that with both curl and Python without success.\n\nThe consistent \"params error\" response is puzzling. I should verify the request headers and body format are correct, or try a minimal test case without any file data to see if the API itself is accessible. Looking at the curl output more closely, the request body shows 205k bytes being sent, yet the server is rejecting it with a parameter error. This suggests either the Authorization header format is incorrect or the Content-Type header is missing or malformed in a way that's causing the server to reject the entire request.\n\nSince all my upload attempts are failing, I should pivot to a different approach. The core issue is that I need to add an image to the record's \"原图\" field, but I can't upload the file directly due to these API errors. Instead, I could update the record to include the image's file token if I can obtain one through a different method. Alternatively, I could try using the bitable API's batch update endpoint to update the record after a successful file upload, though I'd need to first successfully upload the file to get its token. As a simpler workaround, I could create a new record that includes the image directly rather than trying to attach it afterward. for a single record. Maybe the record can only be updated once with an attachment if the attachment is provided at record creation time? No, that doesn't make sense.\n\nLet me try one more thing - use the Feishu API directly but with the file token from a different approach. Wait - I could try to get the image uploaded to a chat message first, then use that file_token. But that's circular.\n\nOK I'm going to give up on the image upload for now and just confirm the text record was created successfully. The user can add the image manually if needed. But let me try ONE more API approach - maybe the issue is the Authorization header format. Let me try with a rawcurl command or check if the token has any invisible characters:","thinkingSignature":"aa110e615771db4f0b37f961d9cead38a04c42f545eb24362ffda156fc57e788"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ox8y3bje62cl_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\")')\n# Check token length and check for any issues\necho \"Token length: ${#TOKEN}\"\n# Check if token looks valid (should start with eyJ and end with signature)\necho \"First 10 chars: ${TOKEN:0:10}\"\necho \"Last 10 chars: ${TOKEN: -10}\"\n# Try echo to see if there's hidden chars\necho \"Token: $TOKEN\" | wc -c"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":71099,"output":834,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":100317,"cost":{"input":0.0213297,"output":0.0010008,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02403354}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709346194,"responseId":"06171d6264c2dce4441ab54f38648dd1"}}
