{"type":"message","id":"b4e4e5f3","parentId":"8b65963b","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:49:51.731Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the token is being extracted correctly (2307 chars, starts with eyJ, ends with 4Gz88CvVdg). \n\nWait, I just realized something important. The Feishu API error \"params error\" with code 1061002 - looking at this error code, it might mean the API parameters are wrong in a specific way. Let me try to look at what the exact issue might be.\n\nActually, I just realized something. When I look at the curl output earlier:\n```\n< HTTP/1.1 100 Continue\n< HTTP/1.1 200 OK\n< content-type: application/json\n```\n\nThe server responded with 100 Continue AND then 200 OK to the same request! But the body was `{\"code\":1061002,\"msg\":\"params error.\"}`. \n\nThat's really odd - a 200 status with an error response. But thinking about it more, the 100 Continue is just the server acknowledging it can receive large files, and the 200 OK with an error body suggests the request actually succeeded in reaching the server, but the \"params error\" is Feishu's way of saying something about the actual request parameters was invalid. Given that both curl and Python urllib are consistently getting this same error regardless of approach, and the token is valid, I'm suspecting the issue is with one of the required parameters like `file_type`, `parent_type`, or `parent_node`.\n\nLet me test with a minimal set of parameters to isolate which one is causing the problem, or maybe I'm using the wrong API endpoint entirely - Feishu might have separate endpoints for drive files versus media files.","thinkingSignature":"fe146f6da6a1374d8c55f706ab214843f450a6e750c107e4125169a7dd54b168"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cqnyl0dz7loy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Try with almost no optional params - just the minimum\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}\" \\\n  -F \"file_name=test.jpg\" \\\n  -F \"file_type=image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_type=bitable_image\" \\\n  -F \"parent_node=TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1\" \\\n  -F \"file=@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":72239,"output":573,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":101196,"cost":{"input":0.0216717,"output":0.0006876,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.024062339999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709376825,"responseId":"06171d8010e0917643170d71b02bd6f8"}}
