{"type":"message","id":"9db379b5","parentId":"06a25c16","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:57:01.863Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to check the experience from this morning - they mentioned that it worked in the morning. Let me look at the memory file and the skill documentation to find what worked this morning.\n\nLooking at the summary, the key breakthrough was using `feishu_doc_media` tool with `bitable_upload` action, and the file had to be in `/tmp/` directory. But the tool wasn't available after Gateway restart.\n\nWait - the user said \"上午都成功了的\" (it worked this morning). Looking at the summary, this morning:\n- We successfully uploaded files using curl to the API endpoint\n- The token was obtained from Keychain\n- We used `files/upload_all` with `extra.bitablePerm`\n\n\n- Now it's failing with a 1061002 \"params error\" when using the same approach\n\nThe issue might be that the user access token has expired - in the morning it was valid but now it's returning an invalid token error, which is different from the parameter error we saw before.\n\nWait, actually in the morning the upload also initially failed before we got it working. The summary mentions that `feishu_doc_media` with `bitable_upload` worked when the file was in `/tmp/`, so let me try using that tool instead of trying to fix the curl approach.","thinkingSignature":"6521cbdd628f4575c8e6d2e7153cd911d686d83c2fc8cbc16e021ced0a6a1215"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_4tkvq73fqp7w_1","name":"memory_search","arguments":{"query":"bitable_upload 上传 附件 成功 经验"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":304,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":69793,"totalTokens":98608,"cost":{"input":0.0000381,"output":0.0003648,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0.026172375,"total":0.028278315000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709808373,"responseId":"06171f3002ff3df1ec495b579e