{"type":"message","id":"7f5c4e01","parentId":"1afdea8c","timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:59:31.882Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see it! The parentType is set to `'bitable_image'` for images and `'bitable_file'` for files. And it passes this to the SDK call.\n\nThe SDK call in the code is:\n```javascript\nsdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n    data: {\n        file_name: fileName,\n        parent_type: parentType,\n        parent_node: p.app_token,\n        size: fileSize,\n        file: fileBuffer,\n        extra: JSON.stringify({\n            bitablePerm: {\n                tableId: p.table_id,\n            },\n        }),\n    },\n}, opts), { as: 'user' });\n```\n\nNotice that `extra` is a JSON string, not an object. And importantly, in the SDK call, `extra` is passed as a STRINGIFIED JSON, not as an object. My curl calls were passing `extra` as a JSON string (using `json.dumps` in Python or `echo` with JSON in shell), so that should be correct.\n\nBut wait - looking at the curl call, I'm passing `extra` as a form field with the stringified JSON, which matches what the SDK is doing. So that's not the issue either. Let me check if there's something else I'm missing about how the SDK handles the file buffer versus how curl sends the file data.\n\nActually, I think the problem might be with the file buffer itself. When Node reads a file with `fs.readFile`, it returns a Buffer, but when curl sends a file with `@/tmp/geography_q25.jpg`, it's sending the raw binary data. These should be equivalent, but maybe the API expects a specific format or encoding. Let me reconsider - the issue could be that the SDK call structure or the way the data is being formatted for the request body is different from what curl is doing.","thinkingSignature":"24e1b10bab212de5d74c1854a5e921b3bae20a970b501a08271f614e7d8b52b7"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ijee9ptvmdn7_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s 'openclaw-feishu-uat' -a 'cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83' -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); print(d.get(\"accessToken\",\"\"))')\n\n# Write a proper node.js script to call the SDK\ncat > /tmp/feishu_upload.js << 'EOF'\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst https = require('https');\n\nconst token = process.env.FEISHU_TOKEN;\nconst filePath = '/tmp/geography_q25.jpg';\nconst stats = fs.statSync(filePath);\nconst fileSize = stats.size;\nconst fileName = path.basename(filePath);\n\nconst extra = JSON.stringify({\n    bitablePerm: {\n        tableId: 'tblJ7fKHxchaECKz',\n        fieldId: 'fld2F4ad3r',\n        recordId: 'recvfaO6GVjeG4'\n    }\n});\n\n// Build multipart form data manually\nconst boundary = '----WebKitFormBoundary' + Math.random().toString(36).substring(2);\nconst fileContent = fs.readFileSync(filePath);\n\nconst parts = [\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file_name\"\\r\\n\\r\\n${fileName}`,\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file_type\"\\r\\n\\r\\nimage`,\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"parent_type\"\\r\\n\\r\\nbitable_image`,\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"parent_node\"\\r\\n\\r\\nTAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1`,\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"size\"\\r\\n\\r\\n${fileSize}`,\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"extra\"\\r\\n\\r\\n${extra}`,\n    `--${boundary}\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"${fileName}\"\\r\\nContent-Type: image/jpeg\\r\\n\\r\\n`\n];\n\nconst body = parts.join('\\r\\n') + fileContent.toString('binary') + `\\r\\n--${boundary}--\\r\\n`;\n\nconst options = {\n    hostname: 'open.feishu.cn',\n    path: '/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all',\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: {\n        'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`,\n        'Content-Type': `multipart/form-data; boundary=${boundary}`,\n        'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body)\n    }\n};\n\nconst req = https.request(options, (res) => {\n    let data = '';\n    res.on('data', chunk => data += chunk);\n    res.on('end', () => {\n        console.log('Status:', res.statusCode);\n        console.log('Response:', data);\n    });\n});\n\nreq.on('error', e => console.error('Error:', e));\nreq.write(body);\nreq.end();\nEOF\n\nFEISHU_TOKEN=\"$TOKEN\" node /tmp/feishu_upload.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":75780,"output":1096,"cacheRead":28384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":105260,"cost":{"input":0.022733999999999997,"output":0.0013151999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0017030399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.025752239999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774709945283,"responseId":"06171fb9b3031f748296b1a9fe549021"}}
